WEBVTT

00:11:59.093 --> 00:12:02.516
And then the next thing you know,
I'm traveling to Tahiti and to Europe

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:04.827
to study in the botanical
gardens of Amsterdam,

00:12:04.851 --> 00:12:07.387
and I'm making up
a 19th-century female botanist

00:12:07.411 --> 00:12:09.144
and I'm writing a novel about it.

00:12:09.168 --> 00:12:12.798
And this is why I say that the path
of curiosity is the scavenger hunt,

00:12:12.822 --> 00:12:14.759
because it took me probably three years

00:12:14.783 --> 00:12:18.121
to get from, "Gee, it would be nice
to put some plants in my backyard,"

00:12:18.145 --> 00:12:21.166
to "Here I am in the South Pacific
exploring the history of moss

00:12:21.190 --> 00:12:23.042
and inventing this giant novel."

00:12:23.066 --> 00:12:26.269
I think everybody thinks that
creativity comes in lightning strikes,

00:12:26.293 --> 00:12:27.952
but I think it comes in whispers,

00:12:27.976 --> 00:12:31.330
and then the whispers
can grow thunderous over time